.-
help for ^hotegfun^                                            [Stata Journal XX]
.-

Multivariate Hotelling test for growth comparison 
-------------------------------------------------

     ^hotegfun^  S1 S2 P1 P2 N1 N2 CL


S1 and S2 are the variance-covariance matrices for (three parameter) growth 
	function (von Bertalanffy, Gomperz, Logistic) for each fish population

P1 and P2 are the (three) parameter column vectors for each fish population

N1 and N2 are the corresponding sample sizes

CL is the desired confidence level (i.e. 99)

Description
-----------

This program performs the multivariate test for comparing growth functions 
(von Bertalanffy, Gomperz, Logistic), considering Hotelling's T^2 statistic
(based on Bernard, D.R. 1981. Multivariate analysis as a means of 
comparing growth in fish. Canadian Journal of Fisheries and Aquatic 
Sciences, 38; 223-236). It displays a table with the results.


Remarks
-------


All seven arguments must be entered in order to perform the test. The 
required matrices may be entered or obtained by nl vbgf, nl gom3, or 
nl log3. 

This program uses corrected expressions from Bernard (1981) which has
several misprints.


Examples
--------

Inputting the matrices by hand:

. ^matrix Sm = (294.74,-0.6018,-32.57\-.6018,.0013,.073\-32.57,.073,4.2296)^

. ^matrix Sf = (1596.18,-1.1895,-91.05\-1.1895,.0009,.0713\-91.0468,.07,5.76)^

. ^matrix Pm=(441.16,.13,-3.36)^

. ^matrix Pf=(505.97,.09,-4.57)^

. ^hotegfun Sm Sf Pm Pf 78 78 99^


Obtaining matrices by nl vbgf

. ^nl vbgf mbl1 age1^

. ^matrix S1 = e(V)^

. ^matrix P1 = e(b)^

. ^display e(N)^
86

. ^nl vbgf mbl2 age2^

. ^matrix S2 = e(V)^

. ^matrix P2 = e(b)^

. ^display e(N)^
78

. ^hotegfun S1 S2 P1 P2 86 78 99^



References
----------

   Bernard, D.R. (1981) Multivariate analysis as a means of comparing growth in
        fish. Canadian Journal of Fisheries and Aquatic Sciences, 38; 223-236.
   Ibanez-Aguirre, A.L., M. Gallardo-Cabello and X. Chiappa-Carrara (1999)
        Growth analysis of striped mullet, Mugil cephalus, and white mullet,
        M. curema (Pisces: Mugilidae), in the Gulf of Mexico. Fishery Bulletin
        97: 861-872.
   Morrison, D.F. (1976) Multivariate statistical methods. 2nd ed. McGraw-Hill
        Book Company, New York, U.S.A. 415 p.
   Salgado-Ugarte, I.H. (1995) Nonparametric methods for fisheries data 
        analysis and their application in conjunction with other statistical 
        techniques to study biological data of the Japanese sea bass 
        Lateolabrax japonicus in Tokyo Bay. PhD on Aquatic Bioscience Thesis 
        dissertation, Tokyo University, Japan. 389 p.
   Salgado-Ugarte, I.H., J. Martinez-Ramirez, J.L. Gomez-Marquez, and B. 
        Pena-Mendoza (2000) sg128. Some programs for growth estimation in 
        fisheries biology. Stata Technical Bulletin 53: 35-47.
   Salgado-Ugarte, I.H., V.M. Saito-Quezada, A. García-Martínez & L. Chacón 
        (2021) Multivariate and likelihood tests for aquatic organisms' growth
	expression comparison. En: De Donato M., González-Henríquez N., 
	Rey-Méndez M., Baltazar-Guerrero P. M., Sonnenholzner J., 
	Alió Mingo J.J., Lodeiros C. 2021. X Foro Iberoamericano de los 
	Recursos Marinos y la Acuicultura: Sinergia entre ciencia e industria
	para el desarrollo y la sostenibilidad. Ediciones AFRIMAR-AFIRMA: 
	1032 pp.  


